From 2568e85a77c1c751624a792853896be67a207be3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 13:56:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 10/33] expert cache: slot_guard() reports the guard applied; a
 test for slot_tail on uniform and sized caches

- ExpertCache::slot_guard() returns the guard open_sized applied (guard_, reset by close), not the request: 0 for
  uniform slots, when closed, and on SYCL, whose open_sized applies none.
- tests/core/expert_cache_slot_guard_test: slot_stride, slot_room and slot_tail on a uniform cache (empty off_,
  including the last slot) and on sized caches with and without the 256 B guard; no guard gives today's offsets;
  close and reopen.
- generate: the "+256 B guard per sized slot" line only for a sized cache; a uniform one says it has no guard.
- prefill: STRATA_MMQ_DIRECT_LOG=1 (with STRATA_MMQ_DIRECT=1) prints each stage's totals of experts read in place,
  resident and streamed after every prompt, so an engine run can show which walk read what.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
